{
  "an5.28:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 5.28 ",
  "an5.28:0.2": "3. With Five Factors ",
  "an5.28:0.3": "With Five Factors ",
  "an5.28:1.1": "“Mendicants, I will teach you how to develop noble right immersion with five factors. ",
  "an5.28:1.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "an5.28:1.3": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "an5.28:1.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an5.28:2.1": "“And how do you develop noble right immersion with five factors? ",
  "an5.28:2.2": "Firstly, a mendicant, quite secluded from sensual pleasures, secluded from unskillful qualities, enters and remains in the first absorption, which has the rapture and bliss born of seclusion, while placing the mind and keeping it connected. ",
  "an5.28:2.3": "They drench, steep, fill, and spread themselves with rapture and bliss born of seclusion. There’s no part of the body that’s not spread with rapture and bliss born of seclusion. ",
  "an5.28:2.4": "It’s like when a deft bathroom attendant or their apprentice pours bath powder into a bronze dish, sprinkling it little by little with water. They knead it until the ball of bath powder is soaked and saturated with moisture, spread through inside and out; yet no moisture oozes out. ",
  "an5.28:2.5": "In the same way, a mendicant drenches, steeps, fills, and spreads themselves with rapture and bliss born of seclusion. ",
  "an5.28:2.6": "There’s no part of the body that’s not spread with rapture and bliss born of seclusion. ",
  "an5.28:2.7": "This is the first